# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081  -  CAT II
# The web server must have Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) that
# invoke OS shell programs disabled.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081
group:           V-206380
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk's static file handler maps an extension to a MIME type and returns
                 the file; it never hands content to a shell. The places where the product
                 will run an operating system program are the script alert action and
                 scripted search commands and REST handlers, and the application can leave
                 the script action unconfigured and unused.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           alert_actions.conf [script] filename empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [] action.script in 0|false

external:        Whether a shell is reachable by the Splunk service account at all, carried
                 by the operating system through the account's shell, the file modes on
                 interpreters, and any mandatory access control policy.
external:        Review of any app-supplied custom search command or scripted REST handler
                 that legitimately invokes an interpreter, carried by the app review
                 procedure; the MIME map itself only names content types for static files
                 and cannot invoke a program (server.conf.spec:1656).

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000081 check and fix text;
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:517 ([script]), alert_actions.conf.spec:518
                 (filename, default empty string), savedsearches.conf.spec:403
                 (action.script, default false), server.conf.spec:1656
                 ([mimetype-extension-map])
finding:         A script is configured for the script alert action, or the script action
                 is enabled on a saved search, so a user of the application can cause an
                 operating system program to run.
